Ah, I like to grind down through the main dungeon very carefully,
gathering up everything, but then rip through Gehennom with magic mapping
- hence I normally need make only one trip back to the stash after the
Castle, to prepare for the final run. Also I establish a secondary cache
at Vlad's - there's boxes lying around, and if the box is next to the
downstairs nothing bad can really happen to it because I'll never wander
around that level - and I'm quite likely to want to pray as part of stash
manipulation.

Also in the middle game it doesn't really hurt to walk up to Sokoban once
or twice - it takes time, but you get a certain amount of Stuff from
whacking beasties en route, and that delays the Castle and hence helps to
increase preparedness. This is a bit artificial - I might as well hang
around scumming one level like an Angband player - but it's less tedious,
and it encourages me to dig a few shortcuts in the main dungeon, which
speeds the escape.
